<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Random episode. Two crossed arrows, drawn as geometry in the control
     bar's language (compare ic_player_switch, the bar's own two-arrow mark)
     instead of the Material shuffle glyph, which is a thin two-curve figure
     with small heads - next to the bar's marks on the same screen it read as
     a different hand entirely.

     Same spec as the rest of the family: 24x24 viewport, bars 2.2 units on
     the 3.4 grid, heads the same isoceles triangles every bar arrow uses
     (4.8 long, 6.8 across the base). The diagonals run at 45 degrees and
     cross on the centre line, so the whole mark stays inside the same
     3.4-unit margin the other glyphs respect. Carries kb_text_hi
     (#FFF3EFE4) baked in, the way every bar glyph does. -->
